Z||000010||sqoach||06-16-2001||06:36 PM||||Very nice car. That red is pretty  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Now, what would make your interior look better? Hmm...how 'bout a short shifter?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach2.JPG">   <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||1
Z||000011||FieroPerformance||06-16-2001||06:54 PM||||Wow, thanks for the compliments guys. Makes me feel all happy inside  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> . You can't tell from the pics but I need a new paint job. There are a few spots where the paint is starting to peal and someone keyed my hood. I want to get a short shifter but it is already hard to shift because the cables are bent a little going around the intake. The guy that owned it before me swapped a 5 speed into it without changing to the Z shaped intake tube so it is kind of stiff shifting and I am afraid that a short shifter would add to the difficulty.<BR>Unfortunately my engine was taken apart for prom so I had to drive the Durango.<BR>The wheels I have are 16" TSW Blades. They don't make them anymore but they sell something similar at <A HREF="http://www.tsw.com" TARGET=_blank>www.tsw.com</A> <P>BTW, today a Porsche 911 Turbo pulled up next to me at a light and wanted to race. My dad was in the car so all I did was look at his car. When the light turned green he chirped his tires and took off like a bat out of hell. O well, at least I can say a $111,000 car thought I was worthy of racing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> .<P>-Charlie<BR>-----<BR>jackalrr@hotmail.com||||reg||1
